<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-25119] .NET: Decimal value scale overflow on representable values</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-25119</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;BigDecimal values like &quot;7.3770697413E+11&quot; or &quot;1E+1&quot;, when inserted from Java and read from .NET, result in an exception:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
Decimal value scale overflow (must be between 0 and 28): -1
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There is even a test for that in &lt;b&gt;TestEchoDecimal&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Those values can be represented in .NET (as 737706974130 and 10, respectively), we should not throw exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
